<p>ClickFunnels made its name by doing one thing extremely well: building sales funnels. It popularised the idea that every business needs a funnel, and it gave non-technical founders a drag-and-drop way to build them. If you have ever clicked on an online course landing page or a "free webinar" signup, there is a good chance ClickFunnels was behind it.</p>

<p>But here is the question worth asking. If you are a small business owner, is a funnel builder enough? Or do you need the other pieces too, the CRM, the email follow-ups, the review requests, the appointment booking, the automations that tie it all together?</p>

<p>That is where this comparison gets interesting. ClickFunnels does funnels. DUSA does funnels and everything else. The question is which approach fits your business better.</p>

<div class="divider">...</div>

<h2>What ClickFunnels does well</h2>

<p>Credit where it is due. ClickFunnels is one of the best funnel builders on the market. Its drag-and-drop editor is polished, the templates are proven, and the community around the product is massive. If your primary goal is to build a high-converting <a href="/blog/sales-funnel-small-business">sales funnel</a>, ClickFunnels gives you a clear path to do that.</p>

<p>The platform has refined the funnel-building process over years. Upsell pages, order bumps, checkout flows, membership areas. For digital product creators and course sellers, ClickFunnels has a well-earned reputation.</p>

<p>The company has also invested heavily in education and community. There are courses, live events, and a whole ecosystem of "funnel hackers" who share templates and strategies. If you are the kind of person who thrives in that community environment, ClickFunnels delivers real value there.</p>

<h2>Where ClickFunnels gets complicated for small business</h2>

<p>The challenge is what happens beyond the funnel. A funnel captures a lead or makes a sale. But then what? You need to follow up with that lead. You need to manage the relationship in a CRM. You need to send emails and SMS. You need to book appointments. You need to request reviews. You need to automate the repetitive parts of all of that.</p>

<p>ClickFunnels has started adding some of these features. Recent versions include a basic CRM, email marketing, and some automation tools. But these are add-ons to a funnel builder, not native features of an integrated platform. They feel bolted on, because they are. If you want to see why <a href="/blog/all-in-one-vs-separate-tools">integrated platforms outperform bolted-together stacks</a>, the difference matters more than it might seem.</p>

<blockquote><p>A great funnel without follow-up is like a great shopfront with nobody behind the counter. You will get attention, but you will not keep it.</p></blockquote>

<p>Then there is the pricing. ClickFunnels Basic starts at $147 USD per month. The Pro plan is $197 per month, and the Funnel Hacker plan is $297 per month. That is $147 to $297 per month for a platform that is primarily a funnel builder. You will still need separate tools for review management, advanced CRM, and features that ClickFunnels does not cover natively.</p>

<h2>Where DUSA takes a different approach</h2>

<p>DUSA was not built as a funnel tool that added other features over time. It was built as a complete growth platform from the start. The funnel builder is one tool among many, sitting alongside CRM, email marketing, SMS, appointment booking, review management, automation, and pipeline management.</p>

<p>That matters in practice because the tools talk to each other natively. When someone fills out a form on your funnel, they appear in your CRM automatically. The automation triggers the right follow-up sequence. The booking link goes out at the right time. The review request fires after the appointment. It is one system, not five tools patched together with integrations.</p>

<p>For small business owners who need <a href="/blog/landing-pages-that-convert">landing pages that convert</a> but also need everything that comes after the conversion, that integration is the real advantage.</p>

